Description: elanmoc: stop listing once every enrolled slot has been read
 elanmoc_list() always walks every storage slot, even when the chip has
 just reported how many are occupied in MOC_LIST_GET_ENROLLED. On a chip
 with one finger enrolled that is ten get-userid round trips instead of
 one, and fprintd runs this list on every failed match (see
 fprintd/src/device.c, "verifying local storage"), i.e. right in the
 login path. Stop as soon as curr_enrolled prints have been collected.
 Counting the prints found rather than the slots queried keeps this
 correct when the occupied slots are not contiguous.
Author: local
Last-Update: 2026-07-30
Index: libfprint-1.95.1+tod1/libfprint/drivers/elanmoc/elanmoc.c
===================================================================
--- libfprint-1.95.1+tod1.orig/libfprint/drivers/elanmoc/elanmoc.c
+++ libfprint-1.95.1+tod1/libfprint/drivers/elanmoc/elanmoc.c
@@ -585,7 +585,13 @@ elanmoc_get_userid_cb (FpiDeviceElanmoc
       g_ptr_array_add (self->list_result, g_object_ref_sink (print));
     }
 
-  if(self->list_index <= ELAN_MAX_ENROLL_NUM)
+  /* The number of occupied slots is known from MOC_LIST_GET_ENROLLED, so stop
+   * as soon as they have all been read instead of always walking every slot.
+   * The slots need not be contiguous, hence counting what was found rather
+   * than how many were queried.
+   */
+  if(self->list_index <= ELAN_MAX_ENROLL_NUM &&
+     self->list_result->len < self->curr_enrolled)
     {
       fpi_ssm_jump_to_state (self->task_ssm, MOC_LIST_GET_FINGER);
     }
